# Allow-list: Docker only receives what the images need. Everything else - data/ and
# retrieval-data/ (many GB), results/, .env (secrets), .git - stays out of the build, which
# keeps builds fast and keeps secrets and data out of the images.
*

!requirements-backend.txt
!requirements-network-sensor.txt
!requirements-retrieval-docker.txt
!.env.example
!security_platform/backend/
!llm/
!security_platform/frontend/
!security_platform/network_sensor/
!threat_retrieval_engine/
!config/
!scripts/docker/retrieval_data.py
!scripts/docker/retrieval_start.py

# Never, even inside the folders above
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.db
**/.pytest_cache
**/.env
